1
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,860
Somehow, it'll work out.

2
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,580
Look, even the burning steel.

5
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll work out somehow, sooner or later.

6
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You understand, right?
I understand, I understand.

7
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,560
Senpai.

9
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:50,060
Damn it! Keirin, pachinko, horse racing...

10
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,860
Nothing's going right today.

11
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,880
But what are we going to do, senpai?

12
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:58,540
You blew through this month's entire paycheck in one day,
didn't you?

13
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,200
Yeah, the paycheck came out yesterday...

14
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,880
So the money I had only lasted a single day?

15
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,700
Anyway, at this rate I'm going to starve.

16
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,180
I have to do something about this.

17
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,800
Get back the lottery tickets!

18
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,600
You idiot!

19
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:20,780
There's no need to yell so loudly, is there?

20
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,700
How could I not yell at this?

21
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:27,720
Asking for an advance just one day after payday,
what is this nonsense?

22
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,900
And you went and lost all of it.

23
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,820
Don't lie, I know you.

24
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,780
You blew it all on bike racing,
pachinko, and horse racing, didn't you?

25
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,660
Wow, you've got it all right.

26
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:38,200
Hey, Bakahonza.

27
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,880
You idiot!

28
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,960
That was especially brutal today, wasn't it?

29
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,080
It rang right through
to the core of my head.

30
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:44,980
But Chief...

31
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:48,260
What am I supposed to
do for the next 29 days?

32
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:50,480
Are you telling me to live on mist?

33
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,380
Right, here's what you'll do.

34
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,920
That's cruel!

35
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,680
That's what I'd like to say, but...

36
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,600
Listen, Ryotsu.

37
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,800
Never gamble again.

38
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:02,540
Put that in writing, and I'll lend you
the money this once as a special favor.

39
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,580
A written pledge?

40
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,580
Right.

41
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:09,420
If you don't write it,
I guess you'll live on mist or tree roots.

42
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,220
You can't survive on that.

43
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:14,720
You really need to eat some rice.

44
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,940
Are you going to write it or not?

45
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:20,020
Fine, I'll write it. Happy now?

46
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:26,560
I, Kankichi Ryotsu, will never gamble again.

47
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:27,980
This is good enough, right?

48
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:38,040
That's not enough. Add this after it:
"If I break this promise and gamble again, I will donate all of the winnings from that gambling..."

49
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:45,620
...I will donate all of it. Fine,
fine, all of it. Any complaints? Got it.

50
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:51,860
Kankichi Ryotsu. Is this good?
Yeah, and the stamp too. Yes.

51
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,060
The stamp

52
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:00,360
Alright, fine.

53
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,760
Then let's get that advance right away.

54
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:03,360
Here.

55
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,060
What's this?

56
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:07,320
It's a ¥2,000 bill.

57
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:08,280
Rare, isn't it.

58
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:10,000
Only ¥2,000?

59
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:12,880
You said you wanted to eat rice, didn't you?

60
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:15,660
With ¥2,000,
you can buy a month's worth of rice.

61
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,640
Make it last somehow, then.

62
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,460
That's ridiculous.

63
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:18,960
No way.

64
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:25,000
Senpai, what do you really
plan to do for a whole month?

65
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:31,360
¥2,000 is nothing. If only this could double,
triple, grow tenfold or a hundredfold.

66
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:36,280
That's impossible. Money doesn't just multiply like clones,
you know.

67
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,540
Was there a bank here?

68
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:45,000
Come, come, everyone who has lost
their dreams in this recession!

69
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,540
Moyashi Bank has just
released a new lottery!

70
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:53,020
Just fill in seven numbers
and your dreams will come true.

71
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:53,820
How about it?

72
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:58,120
Moyashi Bank? What a name.
It sounds like it has no stamina at all.

73
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:00,200
N-no, that's not true at all!

74
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,880
Bean sprouts grow even
where the sun doesn't reach,

75
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,360
and they go with anything.

76
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:07,640
The perfect food for this
recession and layoff era.

77
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:12,240
This bean sprout lottery is
safer than any other lottery.

78
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:14,580
So I just pick seven numbers?

79
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,360
It's just like the Loto lottery, isn't it?

80
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,900
But the Loto has a combination
of six numbers, right?

81
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:23,760
With one more number, the odds are

82
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:26,900
First prize is a whopping four billion yen!

83
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:29,540
What, four billion yen?

84
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:32,220
Yes, the drawing is a week from today.

85
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:35,840
Up until 2:59:59 p.m. the next day,

86
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,780
if you bring your
winning ticket to the bank,

87
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,580
you'll be a dream millionaire!

88
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:40,960
Alright, I won!

89
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:43,960
But senpai, isn't this basically gambling?

90
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,940
It's the same as buying stocks,
which isn't gambling.

91
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,040
Is it?

92
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:52,000
Anyway, you can't live on ¥2000.

93
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,700
I'll bet it all on this.

94
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,720
That's what being a man is all about, right?

95
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,680
So I just mark this one?

96
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,260
Yes.

97
00:05:58,260 --> 00:05:59,960
I'll take ¥2000 worth.

98
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:01,020
Thank you very much.

99
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:04,660
Well, it's all or nothing. Wish me luck.

100
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:07,380
1846497

101
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,060
I hope it'll be okay.

102
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:13,920
Ryo-chan, you've gotten really thin.

103
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:18,380
I hear he's really been living on
nothing but mist and tree roots.

104
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:21,180
That ¥2000 you borrowed from the Chief,

105
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,600
what happened to it, I wonder?

106
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,160
Well...

107
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,980
Alright, let's head out!

108
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:27,840
Are all three of you ready?

109
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:28,300
Yes.

110
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,000
Hey, Ryotsu!

111
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,040
I'm asking if you're ready!

112
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,220
I told you clearly yesterday, didn't I?

113
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:37,520
Yesterday?

114
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,840
Since when is today yesterday,
and until when was yesterday?

115
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:43,880
I'm so hungry I can't make
sense of anything anymore.

116
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,600
Then what about the ¥2000 I lent you?
What did you do with it?

117
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,260
That? I've got it all covered.

118
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:54,160
Where were we headed again?

119
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:58,640
We're going to inspect the security
system of the new bank that just opened.

120
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:01,921
Lately, there've been bank robberies by
thieves who specialize in cracking safes,

121
00:07:01,971 --> 00:07:05,920
and the Napoleons' crimes keep happening,
one after another.

122
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:10,600
Weren't there some comedy
magic duo or something?

123
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,760
That's the Napoleons.

124
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:17,120
Pumpkin Bank lost 8 billion yen,
and Petit Tomato Bank lost 2 billion.

125
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:21,200
Goya Bank was also robbed
of a whopping 5 billion yen.

126
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:26,600
For the sake of the police's honor, we have
to prevent the next robbery before it happens.

127
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:29,220
Somehow, that doesn't quite click.

128
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:31,800
Two thousand yen, and billions of yen,

129
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:34,240
Snap out of it, Ryo-chan.

130
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,960
Senpai, are you all right?

131
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:38,220
What a pathetic fool you are.

132
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:42,220
Pull yourself together, or I'll
leave you locked in the bank's vault!

133
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:50,160
Our bank does business with the Nakagawa Konzern and the Akimoto Group,
among others, so we are a very exclusive institution.

134
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:53,380
We take the utmost care
to guard against crime.

135
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:55,880
Confirmed.

136
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:01,140
As you can see, even boarding the elevator
down to the vault requires verification.

137
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:06,040
The system only lets a handful of
people besides me ride this elevator.

138
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:07,740
Huff, huff.

139
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:09,420
Right this way, please.

140
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:17,060
The vault room is on
the 15th basement floor.

141
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,340
It's safer than a nuclear shelter.

142
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:23,360
This is the vault room.

143
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,200
Wow, this is amazing.

144
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,180
It's the latest model vault, after all.

145
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,080
I'm turning off the infrared sensors now.

146
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:34,080
If you touch these infrared sensors,

147
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:36,140
sleeping gas will immediately spray out

148
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:38,160
and put the thief to sleep.

149
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,840
But you can remember so many passwords?

150
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:45,840
My fingers pretty much remember them.

151
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:47,720
Sensors deactivated.

152
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,220
Alright, let's go.

153
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:51,880
Wow, it's really big up close, isn't it.

154
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:55,120
Next, I'll verify your signed pledge,

155
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:56,960
Confirmed.

156
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:01,820
When the panel opens,
another sensor appears.

157
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:05,420
The one on the right is the sensor that
checks the signature and the passphrase.

158
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:09,240
Time is money, and money is money too.

159
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,600
Confirmed.

160
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,820
That's my personal motto, isn't it.

161
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:17,340
And finally, the sensor on
the left performs a retina scan.

162
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:21,600
Confirmed.

163
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,400
The door will open.

164
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,620
Yes, yes, it's opening.
Please step back a little.

165
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:33,900
Well, unless you make a clone of me,

166
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,940
infiltrating this place is impossible.

167
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:37,520
What an amazing system.

168
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,080
It's pretty spacious inside, too.

169
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,280
I'm so hungry, my eyes are going blurry.

170
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:47,900
What's wrong?

171
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:50,500
I tripped over some kind of box.

172
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:52,460
Wait, what's this?

173
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,880
Aren't these stacks of cash?

174
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,660
That's 100 million yen.

175
00:09:57,660 --> 00:09:59,280
W-what, 100 million!?

176
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:01,260
Don't leave it lying bare
on the floor like that!

177
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:03,600
Someone must have forgotten to put it away.

178
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:05,620
Please just set it aside over there.

179
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:07,960
Well, let's head further inside.

180
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:10,240
There's about 30 billion yen's
worth of gold bullion here.

181
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:14,520
100 million...
if I had this, if I just had this -

182
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,200
Ryotsu

183
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,360
I know, I know.

184
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:22,120
Once I realized it wasn't mine,
it suddenly felt so heavy.

185
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,780
Ryo-chan, you're hopeless.

186
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,480
Of all things,
tripping over a hundred million yen!

187
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,180
That's a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

188
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:31,360
That's because you're not paying attention.

189
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:32,440
Hurry up and come out.

190
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,380
Yeah, yeah.

191
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,900
Then I'm closing it.

192
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:36,400
Okay.

193
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:39,700
No way.

194
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:41,560
You close it manually?

195
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,880
It's locked now.

196
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,940
Now if we just turn on the infrared sensors,

197
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:49,000
no one can get in.

198
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:52,320
With this, we can rest completely easy.

199
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:56,460
And if they do come, it'll be a disaster.

200
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:06,000
Even the Napoleons
couldn't crack that vault.

201
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,920
It should be fine.

202
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,440
Hey, boss, we've got trouble!

203
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,760
Yay!

204
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,340
A pro rider shouldn't fall over like that!

205
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:21,840
Senpai,
about that Moyashi lottery the other day...

206
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,000
Ow

207
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:27,180
Idiot, the Chief will find out!

208
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,180
No, it's not a lottery or anything.

209
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:33,620
Just say you got an upset stomach
from the bean sprout scraps, Honda.

210
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:34,980
Yes, exactly.

211
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:38,740
I thought you were talking about gambling,
whether you win or lose!

212
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:41,800
No way.
Come on, Honda, let's go to the hospital.

213
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:45,900
By the way, Chief,
the lottery is just gambling,

214
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:47,980
You're still saying that?

215
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:51,000
No lottery, no soccer pools, none of it!

216
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:51,520
Yes.

217
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:51,820
Yes.

218
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:53,540
Yes, yes, yes.

219
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:55,960
Did it really win?

220
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,720
Look, look at this.

221
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,460
Where? Where?

222
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:01,660
I circled it in red pencil.

223
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:03,040
The senior officer said so too.

224
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:05,000
All or nothing, all right?

225
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,180
1846497

226
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:08,260
First prize is...

227
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,580
4 billion yen

228
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:13,880
Yahoo!

229
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:15,940
We can live off this
for the rest of our lives!

230
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,820
We did it, senpai!

231
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,560
4 billion!

232
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:20,860
4 billion!

233
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:23,320
4 billion! 4 billion!

234
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,400
No, no, no...

235
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,560
Senpai, the first prize...

236
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,241
Back then,

237
00:12:29,291 --> 00:12:32,960
I said that if I ever gambled,
I'd donate all the profits.

238
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,180
That's right!

239
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:38,440
Listen, Honda,
don't tell the Chief about this.

240
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:41,910
Once we grab 4 billion and run overseas,

241
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,240
it's ours!

242
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:46,080
That's right, Honda,
I'll give you 400 million!

243
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,280
No, no, 400 million is peanuts!

244
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:50,880
In return, keep quiet around the Chief.

245
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,380
Yes, sir! Let's go cash it in right away!

246
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,340
Right, we'd better hurry.

247
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:58,400
Wait, was it this way?

248
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,980
W-wh-what, s-senpai?

249
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:04,120
Wh-wh-wh-wh-wh-wh

250
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:06,460
No way...

251
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,760
W-wh-wh-wh-what?

252
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,740
N-no way... you don't mean...

253
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:12,080
It's gone!

254
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:12,920
Hey!

255
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:16,400
It was right here a moment ago,
and now it's gone!

256
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:18,300
N-no way...

257
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:20,380
Where did you drop it?

258
00:13:20,380 --> 00:13:21,920
Think back, please.

259
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:25,080
It was then.

260
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:27,320
